Z||000000||lennyb4||04-27-2000||09:45 AM||||Ladies and gentlemen,<P> I have solved the ever elusive beverage holder problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> For those of you who are familar w/the chevy lumina (97-99). They came w/a slide out dual cup holder that mounts under the ash tray. Well i have sucessfully gratfed this into the fiero. This can be done anywhere you have the clearance. I placed mine above my after market stereo. Looks real good. Ill try to get some pics and post them.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cooter||04-27-2000||03:41 PM||||Hmmm. Above the radio? I worked on a lot of Honda stereos that got filled with cola and coffee because the early 90's had the cup holder above the radio. A good bump and it is time for a garden hose to the stereo!||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||04-27-2000||11:29 PM||||Very interesting!  How does it mount? The future Mrs stimpy thought a slide out dual cup holder mounted  under the dash on the passengers side would be keen. Do you think that it would mount up like that? Do you have part # or pics?  ||||reg||5
Z||000003||lennyb4||04-28-2000||08:43 AM||||First it wouldnt spill on the stereo because the cup is about 2" in front of the faceing. And yes you can mount it anywhere (with a little imagination). I dont have the factory part numbers. I took mine off a wrecked one in the bone yard. Im trying to get a dig. camera so i can take some pics.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||04-28-2000||08:55 AM||||I snapped a picture of a very intersting cup holder at the Daytona Fiero Show last month.  I had forgotten about it, but sometime this weekend Ill scan it and post for all to see.  Its pretty cool, and appeared to be able to handle not one but <B>two</B> big gulps with no problem!<P>And its radio friendly...||||reg||1
Z||000005||zeusrekning||04-28-2000||11:46 PM||||no no no I have got the best cup holder in my 87 fiero. Her name is tab. We have been dating for over a year and she can hold any size drink I buy from a can to a 3 liter. And she has only spilled one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> true she is not always in the car.||||reg||1
